# Home lab node registry — hybrid provider (ADR-046 §13)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Format (one line per Flatcar Hyper-V worker node):
#   <hostname>|<ssh-target>|<wsl-distro>|<tailnet-host>|<box-tag>|<target-cluster>|<startupGB>|<minGB>|<maxGB>|<cpus>|<diskGB>
#
# Fields:
#   hostname      : kubernetes node hostname (derived by the provisioner as
#                   flatcar-node-<idx>; the first field is informational)
#   ssh-target    : user@ip or user@hostname for SSH access from the Mac to the
#                   Windows host (provision-flatcar-worker.sh drives Hyper-V
#                   over PowerShell via this SSH session)
#   wsl-distro    : legacy field, informational only (WSL2 era)
#   tailnet-host  : Tailscale MagicDNS hostname (derived as
#                   flatcar-node-<idx>.<tailnet>; informational)
#   box-tag       : human label for the physical box (box-a, box-b, etc.)
#   target-cluster: destination cluster: 'hub' (Hub management cluster) or
#                   'spoke' (Spoke tenant cluster).
#   startupGB     : VM startup memory in GB (default Hyper-V sizing, auto)
#   minGB         : dynamic memory floor in GB (min==startup==max => static)
#   maxGB         : dynamic memory ceiling in GB
#   cpus          : virtual CPU count
#
# Capacity is read from this registry by default — no CLI flags required;
# the provisioner is driven solely by `--node N` (N = 1-based registry index).
#
# IMPORTANT: Copy this file to home-lab.env and fill in real values.
# home-lab.env is gitignored; this example ships safe placeholders.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Box A: Primary workstation (Dual-VM or Dedicated Hub Worker)
HOME_WORKER_NODES="flatcar-hub-node-1|user@REPLACE_IP|unused|flatcar-hub-node-1.REPLACE_TAILNET.ts.net|box-a|hub|6|6|6|4"

# Box A or Box B: Spoke workload worker
HOME_WORKER_NODES="$HOME_WORKER_NODES
flatcar-spoke-node-1|user@REPLACE_IP|unused|flatcar-spoke-node-1.REPLACE_TAILNET.ts.net|box-a|spoke|4|4|4|4"

# Tailscale tailnet name (e.g. example.ts.net)
TAILNET_NAME="REPLACE_TAILNET.ts.net"

# Hybrid spoke pool name (matches the SpokePool claim name)
HYBRID_SPOKE_NAME="spoke-pool-hybrid-dev-01"

# Hub kubeconfig path (used by the provisioner to read spoke kubeconfig)
# NOTE: The hybrid dev hub is "hub-hybrid-dev.kubeconfig" — "hub.kubeconfig"
# does not exist. Use whatever kubeconfig file was emitted for the environment.
# Respect a caller-supplied value: the bootstrap orchestrator runs this script
# before pivot has written the canonical kubeconfig, and needs to point it
# elsewhere. Unconditional assignment here silently overrides that.
HUB_KUBECONFIG="${HUB_KUBECONFIG:-${ZERO_OPS_DIR:-$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)}/k8-secrets/kubeconfig/hub-hybrid-dev.kubeconfig}"